SYNTHESIS
==============================================================================
1. HYP-2025's full-support NZ flow is one layer of a larger support-flow
   enumerator: every nonzero Fourier support is a NZ flow on a sub-dipole.
2. On the dual cover graph, a positive lonely interval is a zero-flow cut
   in the danger-arc coverage flow.  AP walls are nowhere-zero on open
   cells but have empty strict endpoint-protection cores.
3. A true counterexample would need both sides at once: full cancellation
   of the support-flow enumerator and a nonpeeling nowhere-zero cover-flow
   core with best margin below 1/n.  That is much more rigid than merely
   having many full-support resonances.
